<title>UK: Rolls-Royce wins 55 mln stg RAF service deal.</title>
<headline>Rolls-Royce wins 55 mln stg RAF service deal.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Rolls-Royce Plc said on Thursday that it has won a 10 year contract to  provide maintenance support for the Royal Air Force's Adour engines, worth around 55 million stg.</p>
<p>The agreement is between Rolls-Royce Aero Engine Services Ltd and the Ministry of Defence.</p>
<p>Adour engines power the RAF Valley-based Hawk trainer fleet and the RAF's complement of Jaguars based at Coltishall, Norfolk in eastern England and Lossiemouth, Scotland.</p>
<p>-- Reuter Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
